  <!--
    MudAlert: `<Border Classes="alert">`, from _alert.scss. Variant.Text is the default; `outlined`
    and `filled` switch it, and a colour class is the Severity (`info`, `success`, `warning`,
    `error`, and any other palette colour). With no colour it is Severity.Normal: text-primary on
    dark-hover. Text and outlined alerts draw their TEXT in the colour's darken shade and only the
    icon in the colour itself; filled ones are the colour with its contrast text, at weight 500.
    The colour is inherited, so put the message and a PathIcon inside and both follow it.
    `dense` is `.mud-dense`: 0 12px.

    The padding is `.mud-alert`'s 6px with `.mud-alert-message`'s 9px inside it: a Border has one
    padding for whatever the app puts in it, so a one-line alert is MudAlert's 50px. An icon is
    `.mud-alert-icon`: 24px, 12px before the message, at .9 opacity, and on the first line, as
    `.mud-alert-position` aligns to the start - its 7px padding puts it 2px above the text's 9px.
    The 24px is the MudIcon's own `.mud-icon-size-medium` (1.5rem, _icons.scss; MudIcon.razor.cs
    defaults Size to Medium), which overrides `.mud-alert-icon`'s 22px font-size on the svg itself:
    7 + 24 + 7 is the message's 9 + 20 + 9.
